-- ============================================================================
-- FC5 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Relief & Flare Systems, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE FIRE CASE AND THE DRUM. Where a relief load comes
-- from and what the engine leaves to the caller; the wetted area as an exact
-- circular segment lying down and a cylinder standing up; the pool fire duty
-- and the drainage credit; the fire case end to end, from level to letter; and
-- the flare knockout drum, where the liquid level sets both the vapour area and
-- the fall distance.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. The holdup MOVES the drum length. The level
-- sets the vapour cross-section as the circular segment above it and the fall
-- distance as the vapour depth, two different functions of one fraction, so a
-- reader who uses one factor for both has a drum that is exactly right at half
-- full and wrong everywhere else.
--
-- The fire DUTY is never graded: 21000, 34500 and the 0.82 exponent are held
-- for literature. The capstone grades the GEOMETRY the duty stands on, and the
-- drum states its own dropout velocity and actual vapour rate, so no graded
-- value reads the sphere-drag correlation or a standard-condition base.
-- ============================================================================

